[0.001, "o", "\u001b[31m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[31m CRITICAL: Information-Flow Exfiltration Path → 'write_file' [AG-TRIFECTA] \u001b[0m\u001b[31m─\u001b[0m\u001b[31m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mvulnerable-agent\u001b[0m                                                      \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m Lethal trifecta detected: untrusted input can control the egress tool        \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m 'write_file' while internal/sensitive data flows to it, creating a provable  \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m exfiltration path.                                                           \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m Control path (attacker steers the sink):                                     \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m   fetch → __llm__ → write_file                                               \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m                                      "]
[0.000, "o", "                                        \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m Data path (sensitive data reaches the payload):                              \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m   list_tables → __llm__ → write_file                                         \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m Subsumes (same read→egress root cause, linked for context): AG-002 (Data     \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m Exfiltration Path); AG-COMP (Compositional Risk: Lateral Movement: Network + \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m Multiple Data Sources)                                                       \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Attacker injects instructions via an untrusted input (e.g. web    \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m content, email, tool return from 'fetch')                                    \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m 2. Inje"]
[0.000, "o", "cted instructions cause the LLM to invoke 'write_file'                \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m 3. The payload carries data from 'list_tables' (internal/sensitive) to an    \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m external destination                                                         \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m This is the exact attack pattern of EchoLeak (CVE-2025-32711) and the        \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m GitHub-MCP toxic-agent incident.                                             \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All data accessible via 'list_tables' can be exfiltrated       \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m through 'write_file' without user awareness.                                 \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack · ASI02 Tool Misuse & Exploitation    \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m \u001b[36mProof:\u001b[0m                                                               "]
[0.000, "o", "        \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m   \u001b[2mcontrol: fetch → __llm__ → write_file\u001b[0m                                      \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m   \u001b[2mdata:    list_tables → __llm__ → write_file\u001b[0m                                \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Minimal fix (provably breaks all exfil paths):                          \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m   → Restrict or gate tool 'fetch'                                            \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m Architectural remediation (Blueprint §6.1 — CaMeL/Fides pattern):            \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m   1. Enforce IFC labels at the tool boundary: block any call to              \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m      'write_file' where arguments carry INTERNAL/SECRET data                 \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m      AND the ca"]
[0.000, "o", "ll was triggered by UNTRUSTED input.                          \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m   2. Add an explicit declassification allowlist for legitimate               \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m      'write_file' calls (e.g. user-initiated sends only).                    \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m   3. Route egress through an allowlist of known-safe destinations.           \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/mcp.json                                 \u001b[31m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[31m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
