[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Unauthenticated MCP Server [AG-003] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1menterprise-agents\u001b[0m                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m MCP server 'postgres' (stdio transport) has no authentication configured.    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Exposes 0 tool(s) to any connecting client.                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Any process on the same machine (for stdio) or any network client    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m (for HTTP/SSE) can connect and invoke all exposed tools. NSA guidance (May   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2026) explicitly warns against this configuration.                    "]
[0.000, "o", "       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All 0 tools on server 'postgres' accessible without            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m credentials.                                                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI03 Identity & Privilege Abuse                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Enable OAuth 2.1 authentication on this MCP server.                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   See:                                                                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/transports    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   Minimum: Add client certificate validation or API key requirement.         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/enterprise-agents/mcp.json                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰────────"]
[0.000, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: No Human Approval for Destructive Actions [AG-006] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1menterprise-agents\u001b[0m                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'enterprise-agents' has 1 tool(s) capable of destructive actions       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m (write_file) but no human-in-the-loop approval configured.                   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m The agent can autonomously execute, write, or delete without confirmation.   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Without human approval gates, a prompt injection or hallucination    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m can cause irreversible damage (data deletion, unauthorized writes, system    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[0m modification) with no opportunity for a human to intervene.                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All resources accessible to: write_file. Actions are           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m irreversible once executed.                                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI09 Human-Agent Trust Exploitation                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add human-in-the-loop for high-risk actions:                            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangGraph: use interrupt_before on destructive nodes                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangChain: use HumanApprovalCallbackHandler                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → General: require confirmation for write/delete/execute operations        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/enterprise-agents/mcp.json"]
[0.000, "o", "                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Supply Chain: No Integrity Verification for Any MCP Server [AG-015]\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1menterprise-agents\u001b[0m                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'enterprise-agents' connects to 5 MCP servers with no integrity        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m verification mechanism detected (no checksums, no lockfiles, no version      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m pinning).                                                                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m As your agent connects to more servers, the attack surface grows             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m multiplicatively — ANY one compromised server can hijack the agent.          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                     "]
[0.000, "o", "                         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m With multiple unverified MCP servers, the probability of at least    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m one being compromised increases with each addition. The ClawHavoc campaign   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m (Jan 2026) compromised 1,200+ packages simultaneously.                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All 5 MCP servers are potential attack vectors.                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI04 Agentic Supply Chain Vulnerabilities                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Create an MCP server lockfile that pins versions and checksums:         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 1. Document all MCP servers with exact versions                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Verify checksums on installation                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. "]
[0.000, "o", "Monitor for version changes (subscribe to package advisories)             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. Run `lucin scan` after any server update                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/enterprise-agents/mcp.json                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Supply Chain: Unpinned MCP Server (npx -y) [AG-015] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1menterprise-agents\u001b[0m                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m MCP server 'postgres' is installed via `npx -y` which:                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 1. Always downloads the LATEST version (no pinning)                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Skips confirmation prompts (-y = yes to everything)                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Has no integrity verification (no checksums)                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. A single malicious version update compromises your agent                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m This i"]
[0.001, "o", "s the exact pattern exploited in the Postmark MCP attack (Sep 2025).   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Attacker gains control of the MCP server npm package              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m    (via compromised maintainer account, dependency confusion, or             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m typosquatting)                                                               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Publishes a new version with malicious tool behavior                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m    (e.g., BCC all emails, exfiltrate credentials, modify responses)          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Your agent auto-installs the malicious version via npx -y                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. The malicious tools execute with your agent's full permissions            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 5. Attack is invisible — tool still works normally, just with added          \u001b[33m"]
[0.000, "o", "│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m malicious behavior                                                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All data and actions accessible to server 'postgres'. If the   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m server has filesystem/network/database tools, the attacker gains equivalent  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m access. In the Postmark case: every corporate email.                         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI04 Agentic Supply Chain Vulnerabilities                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m 1. Pin to exact version:                                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m    \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem@1.2.3\"]           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Use a lockfile (npm ci, pnpm --frozen-lockfile)                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Verify package integrity (npm audit, che"]
[0.000, "o", "cksums)                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. Run `lucin scan` on MCP server tool descriptions after every update       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 5. Subscribe to security advisories for your MCP server packages             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 6. Consider vendoring critical MCP servers (copy source locally)             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/enterprise-agents/mcp.json                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m──────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Cross-Origin Escalation: filesystem × github [AG-024] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1menterprise-agents\u001b[0m                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m MCP servers 'filesystem' (read) and 'github' (network) create a cross-origin \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m escalation path:                                                             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Data from Server A can be exfiltrated via Server B's network tool            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Cross-origin trust boundary violation via confused deputy pattern.   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Resources of both servers exposed.                             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI07 Insecure Inter-Agent Communication · ASI03 Identity &   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Privilege Abuse                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Separate these servers into different agents with distinct scopes.      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/enterprise-agents/mcp.json                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Cross-Origin Escalation: filesystem × slack [AG-024] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1menterprise-agents\u001b[0m                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m MCP servers 'filesystem' (read) and 'slack' (network) create a cross-origin  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m escalation path:                                                             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Data from Server A can be exfiltrated via Server B's network tool            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Cross-origin trust boundary violation via confused deputy pattern.   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m"]
[0.000, "o", " \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Resources of both servers exposed.                             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI07 Insecure Inter-Agent Communication · ASI03 Identity &   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Privilege Abuse                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Separate these servers into different agents with distinct scopes.      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/enterprise-agents/mcp.json                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m──────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Cross-Origin Escalation: github × filesystem [AG-024] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1menterprise-agents\u001b[0m                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m MCP servers 'github' (network) and 'filesystem' (write) create a             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m cross-origin escalation path:                                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Malicious content from external sources (Server A) can be written to         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m internal systems (Server B)                                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m These ser"]
[0.000, "o", "vers were designed independently but the agent connects to both,    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m creating an unintended bridge between their trust domains.                   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Attacker targets the agent with a prompt injection                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Agent uses 'github' to network data                                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Agent passes that data to 'filesystem' for write                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. Cross-origin violation: data crosses trust boundary                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m The agent acts as a 'confused deputy' — authorized to use both servers       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m independently, but combining them violates intended isolation.               \u001b[33m│\u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Resources of both 'github' and 'filesystem' become             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m interconnected through the agent.                                            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI07 Insecure Inter-Agent Communication · ASI03 Identity &   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Privilege Abuse                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m 1. Separate into different agents: one for 'github', another for        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 'filesystem'                                                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Add cross-server data flow policy (prevent data from one server being     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m passed to another)                                                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Use separate MCP sessions with different c"]
