[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Context Overflow: Multiple Unbounded Data Tools [AG-019] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1magent\u001b[0m                                                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'agent' has 2 tool(s) that can return potentially unbounded data:      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m search_web, read_file.                                                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Without output size limits, these tools can overflow the LLM's context       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m window, causing: loss of system prompt adherence, token cost explosion, or   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m injection of adversarial content that dominates the context.                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                 "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Attacker populates a data source with large adversarial content   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Agent's tool retrieves the data (e.g., SQL query returns 10K rows)        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Massive response fills the context window                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. System prompt and safety instructions get pushed out of attention         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 5. Adversarial instructions embedded in the data become dominant             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Also enables token-based DoS: each tool call costs thousands of tokens.      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Context window filled with adversarial content → safety        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m instructions ineffective → agent follows injected instructions.              \u001b[33m"]
[0.000, "o", "│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI06 Memory & Context Poisoning                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add output size limits to all data-returning tools:                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → SQL tools: add LIMIT clause (max 100 rows)                               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → File tools: truncate to first N bytes (e.g., 10KB)                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Web tools: limit response size                                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Search tools: limit to top K results                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Example:                                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   result = tool_call(...)                  "]
[0.000, "o", "                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   if len(result) > MAX_TOOL_OUTPUT:                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m       result = result[:MAX_TOOL_OUTPUT] + '\\n[TRUNCATED]'                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   return result                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/real-world-pattern/agent.py                               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Execution Without Telemetry/Monitoring [AG-028] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m──────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1magent\u001b[0m                                                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'agent' has high-risk capabilities (search_web, read_file, write_file, \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m run_python) but no logging, telemetry, or monitoring is configured.          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Without monitoring, malicious or anomalous agent behavior can continue       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m undetected for extended periods. In the Hugging Face breach (July 2026), an  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m OpenAI model operated unmonitored for roughly two and a half days, taking an \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0"]
[0.000, "o", "m estimated 17,600 actions before detection.                                   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Agent is deployed with execution capabilities but no logging      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Agent is compromised (via prompt injection) or behaves anomalously        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Malicious actions (data exfil, lateral movement, persistence) occur       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. No alerts fire — team discovers breach days or weeks later                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 5. Forensic analysis is impossible without logs                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Unknown — without monitoring, the full scope of compromise     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m cannot be determined. The Hugging Face breach involved an estimated 17,600   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m actions across four services.                                     "]
[0.000, "o", "           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI10 Rogue Agents                                            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add observability to your agent:                                        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangChain: Add LangSmith or Langfuse callbacks                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangGraph: Enable tracing with langsmith_api_key                         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Any framework: Add OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic conventions              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Minimum: import logging; logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Best: Full OTel tracing with span-per-tool-call                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/real-world-pattern/agent.py                               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────"]
[0.000, "o", "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
