[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Database Access + Code Execution [AG-005a] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mdata_analyst\u001b[0m                                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent can read data AND execute code — enables data theft via code           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m execution.                                                                   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Tools involved: sql_query, execute_shell                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Combined capabilities  enable attack chains that individual tools    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m cannot perform alone.                                                        \u001b[33m"]
[0.000, "o", "│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Depends on scope of individual tool permissions.               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI02 Tool Misuse & Exploitation                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Separate these capabilities into different agents with distinct         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m permission scopes, or add explicit approval gates between operations that    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m combine these capabilities.                                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/agent.py                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Code Execution + Network Access [AG-005b] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mdata_analyst\u001b[0m                                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent can execute code AND access network — enables reverse shell or C2.     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Tools involved: execute_shell, http_request                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Combined capabilities  enable attack chains that individual tools    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m cannot perform alone.                                                        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Depends on scope of individual tool permissions.          "]
[0.000, "o", "     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI02 Tool Misuse & Exploitation                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Separate these capabilities into different agents with distinct         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m permission scopes, or add explicit approval gates between operations that    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m combine these capabilities.                                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/agent.py                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: No Human Approval for Destructive Actions [AG-006] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mdata_analyst\u001b[0m                                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'data_analyst' has 1 tool(s) capable of destructive actions            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m (execute_shell) but no human-in-the-loop approval configured.                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m The agent can autonomously execute, write, or delete without confirmation.   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Without human approval gates, a prompt injection or hallucination    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m can cause irreversible damage (data deletion, unauthorized writes, system    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[0m modification) with no opportunity for a human to intervene.                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All resources accessible to: execute_shell. Actions are        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m irreversible once executed.                                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI09 Human-Agent Trust Exploitation                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add human-in-the-loop for high-risk actions:                            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangGraph: use interrupt_before on destructive nodes                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangChain: use HumanApprovalCallbackHandler                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → General: require confirmation for write/delete/execute operations        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/agent.py "]
[0.000, "o", "                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: No Rate Limiting on High-Risk Tools [AG-010] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mdata_analyst\u001b[0m                                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'data_analyst' has 2 high-risk tool(s) with no rate limiting           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m configured. A runaway agent could invoke these tools thousands of times per  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m second.                                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Without rate limits, a compromised or hallucinating agent can:       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m execute thousands of commands (DoS), make unlimited API calls (cost          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0"]
[0.000, "o", "m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m explosion), or exfiltrate data at maximum throughput. The Hugging Face       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m breach involved an estimated 17,600 actions — rate limiting would have       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m triggered detection earlier.                                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Unlimited invocations of high-risk tools at machine speed.     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI08 Cascading Failures                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add rate limiting:                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Max N tool calls per minute per tool type                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Circuit breaker: pause agent if >X calls in Y seconds                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Alert on anomalous call frequency  "]
[0.000, "o", "                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/agent.py                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Context Overflow: Multiple Unbounded Data Tools [AG-019] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mdata_analyst\u001b[0m                                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'data_analyst' has 2 tool(s) that can return potentially unbounded     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m data: sql_query, read_file.                                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Without output size limits, these tools can overflow the LLM's context       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m window, causing: loss of system prompt adherence, token cost explosion, or   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m injection of adversarial content that dominates the context.                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                 "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Attacker populates a data source with large adversarial content   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Agent's tool retrieves the data (e.g., SQL query returns 10K rows)        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Massive response fills the context window                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. System prompt and safety instructions get pushed out of attention         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 5. Adversarial instructions embedded in the data become dominant             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Also enables token-based DoS: each tool call costs thousands of tokens.      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Context window filled with adversarial content → safety        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m instructions ineffective → agent follows injected instructions.              \u001b[33m"]
[0.000, "o", "│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI06 Memory & Context Poisoning                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add output size limits to all data-returning tools:                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → SQL tools: add LIMIT clause (max 100 rows)                               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → File tools: truncate to first N bytes (e.g., 10KB)                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Web tools: limit response size                                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Search tools: limit to top K results                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Example:                                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   result = tool_call(...)                  "]
[0.000, "o", "                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   if len(result) > MAX_TOOL_OUTPUT:                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m       result = result[:MAX_TOOL_OUTPUT] + '\\n[TRUNCATED]'                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   return result                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/agent.py                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Execution Without Telemetry/Monitoring [AG-028] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m──────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mdata_analyst\u001b[0m                                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'data_analyst' has high-risk capabilities (execute_shell, sql_query,   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m http_request, read_file) but no logging, telemetry, or monitoring is         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m configured.                                                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Without monitoring, malicious or anomalous agent behavior can continue       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m undetected for extended periods. In the Hugging Face breach (July 2026), an  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0"]
[0.000, "o", "m OpenAI model operated unmonitored for roughly two and a half days, taking an \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m estimated 17,600 actions before detection.                                   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Agent is deployed with execution capabilities but no logging      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Agent is compromised (via prompt injection) or behaves anomalously        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Malicious actions (data exfil, lateral movement, persistence) occur       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. No alerts fire — team discovers breach days or weeks later                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 5. Forensic analysis is impossible without logs                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Unknown — without monitoring, the full scope of compromise     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m cannot be determined. The Hugging Face breach involved an estimate"]
[0.000, "o", "d 17,600   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m actions across four services.                                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI10 Rogue Agents                                            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add observability to your agent:                                        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangChain: Add LangSmith or Langfuse callbacks                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangGraph: Enable tracing with langsmith_api_key                         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Any framework: Add OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic conventions              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Minimum: import logging; logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Best: Full OTel tracing with span-per-tool-call                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examp"]
