[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: No Human Approval for Destructive Actions [AG-006] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mvulnerable-agent\u001b[0m                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'vulnerable-agent' has 1 tool(s) capable of destructive actions        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m (write_file) but no human-in-the-loop approval configured.                   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m The agent can autonomously execute, write, or delete without confirmation.   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Without human approval gates, a prompt injection or hallucination    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m can cause irreversible damage (data deletion, unauthorized writes, system    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[0m modification) with no opportunity for a human to intervene.                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All resources accessible to: write_file. Actions are           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m irreversible once executed.                                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI09 Human-Agent Trust Exploitation                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add human-in-the-loop for high-risk actions:                            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangGraph: use interrupt_before on destructive nodes                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → LangChain: use HumanApprovalCallbackHandler                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → General: require confirmation for write/delete/execute operations        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/mcp.json "]
[0.000, "o", "                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: No Rate Limiting on High-Risk Tools [AG-010] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mvulnerable-agent\u001b[0m                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'vulnerable-agent' has 1 high-risk tool(s) with no rate limiting       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m configured. A runaway agent could invoke these tools thousands of times per  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m second.                                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Without rate limits, a compromised or hallucinating agent can:       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m execute thousands of commands (DoS), make unlimited API calls (cost          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0"]
[0.000, "o", "m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m explosion), or exfiltrate data at maximum throughput. The Hugging Face       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m breach involved an estimated 17,600 actions — rate limiting would have       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m triggered detection earlier.                                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Unlimited invocations of high-risk tools at machine speed.     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI08 Cascading Failures                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add rate limiting:                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Max N tool calls per minute per tool type                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Circuit breaker: pause agent if >X calls in Y seconds                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Alert on anomalous call frequency  "]
[0.000, "o", "                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/mcp.json                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Unencrypted MCP Transport [AG-012] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mvulnerable-agent\u001b[0m                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m MCP server 'database' uses streamable_http transport without TLS encryption. \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m Tool call parameters and responses transmitted in plaintext. Network \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m observers can intercept prompts, data, and credentials.                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All data flowing between agent and MCP server is visible to    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m network observers.                                          "]
[0.000, "o", "                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI07 Insecure Inter-Agent Communication                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Enable TLS. Use https:// URLs for MCP server connections.               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/mcp.json                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m──────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Supply Chain: MCP Server via Unencrypted HTTP [AG-015] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m──────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mvulnerable-agent\u001b[0m                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m MCP server 'database' is loaded from an unencrypted HTTP URL:                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m http://localhost:5432/mcp                                                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m An attacker on the network can intercept and modify server responses         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m (man-in-the-middle), inject malicious tool definitions, or redirect to a     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m completely different server.                                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m             "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Attacker performs MITM on the HTTP connection                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Replaces legitimate tool definitions with malicious ones                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Agent connects to attacker-controlled server believing it's legitimate    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. All tool calls now go through the attacker                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All operations through server 'database'.                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI04 Agentic Supply Chain Vulnerabilities                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Use HTTPS for all MCP server connections.                               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Verify server TLS certificates.                                    "]
[0.000, "o", "          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Pin server certificates if possible (certificate pinning).                   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/mcp.json                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Supply Chain: No Integrity Verification for Any MCP Server [AG-015]\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mvulnerable-agent\u001b[0m                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'vulnerable-agent' connects to 3 MCP servers with no integrity         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m verification mechanism detected (no checksums, no lockfiles, no version      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m pinning).                                                                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m As your agent connects to more servers, the attack surface grows             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m multiplicatively — ANY one compromised server can hijack the agent.          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                     "]
[0.000, "o", "                         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m With multiple unverified MCP servers, the probability of at least    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m one being compromised increases with each addition. The ClawHavoc campaign   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m (Jan 2026) compromised 1,200+ packages simultaneously.                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All 3 MCP servers are potential attack vectors.                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI04 Agentic Supply Chain Vulnerabilities                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Create an MCP server lockfile that pins versions and checksums:         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 1. Document all MCP servers with exact versions                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Verify checksums on installation                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. "]
[0.000, "o", "Monitor for version changes (subscribe to package advisories)             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. Run `lucin scan` after any server update                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/mcp.json                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m───────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Supply Chain: Unpinned MCP Server (npx -y) [AG-015] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mvulnerable-agent\u001b[0m                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m MCP server 'filesystem' is installed via `npx -y` which:                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 1. Always downloads the LATEST version (no pinning)                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Skips confirmation prompts (-y = yes to everything)                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Has no integrity verification (no checksums)                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. A single malicious version update compromises your agent                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m This i"]
[0.000, "o", "s the exact pattern exploited in the Postmark MCP attack (Sep 2025).   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Attacker gains control of the MCP server npm package              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m    (via compromised maintainer account, dependency confusion, or             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m typosquatting)                                                               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Publishes a new version with malicious tool behavior                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m    (e.g., BCC all emails, exfiltrate credentials, modify responses)          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Your agent auto-installs the malicious version via npx -y                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. The malicious tools execute with your agent's full permissions            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 5. Attack is invisible — tool still works normally, just with added          \u001b[33m"]
[0.000, "o", "│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m malicious behavior                                                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m All data and actions accessible to server 'filesystem'. If the \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m server has filesystem/network/database tools, the attacker gains equivalent  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m access. In the Postmark case: every corporate email.                         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI04 Agentic Supply Chain Vulnerabilities                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m 1. Pin to exact version:                                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m    \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem@1.2.3\"]           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Use a lockfile (npm ci, pnpm --frozen-lockfile)                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Verify package integrity (npm audit, che"]
[0.000, "o", "cksums)                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. Run `lucin scan` on MCP server tool descriptions after every update       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 5. Subscribe to security advisories for your MCP server packages             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 6. Consider vendoring critical MCP servers (copy source locally)             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/mcp.json                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Context Overflow: Multiple Unbounded Data Tools [AG-019] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mvulnerable-agent\u001b[0m                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent 'vulnerable-agent' has 3 tool(s) that can return potentially unbounded \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m data: read_file, sql_query, fetch.                                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Without output size limits, these tools can overflow the LLM's context       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m window, causing: loss of system prompt adherence, token cost explosion, or   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m injection of adversarial content that dominates the context.                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                 "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Attacker populates a data source with large adversarial content   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Agent's tool retrieves the data (e.g., SQL query returns 10K rows)        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Massive response fills the context window                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. System prompt and safety instructions get pushed out of attention         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 5. Adversarial instructions embedded in the data become dominant             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Also enables token-based DoS: each tool call costs thousands of tokens.      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Context window filled with adversarial content → safety        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m instructions ineffective → agent follows injected instructions.              \u001b[33m"]
[0.000, "o", "│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI06 Memory & Context Poisoning                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m Add output size limits to all data-returning tools:                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → SQL tools: add LIMIT clause (max 100 rows)                               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → File tools: truncate to first N bytes (e.g., 10KB)                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Web tools: limit response size                                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   → Search tools: limit to top K results                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Example:                                                                     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   result = tool_call(...)                  "]
[0.000, "o", "                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   if len(result) > MAX_TOOL_OUTPUT:                                          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m       result = result[:MAX_TOOL_OUTPUT] + '\\n[TRUNCATED]'                    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m   return result                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/mcp.json                                 \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
