[0.001, "o", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m──────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m MEDIUM: Cross-Origin Escalation: database × web-fetch [AG-024] \u001b[0m\u001b[33m──────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Agent: \u001b[1mvulnerable-agent\u001b[0m                                                      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m MCP servers 'database' (read) and 'web-fetch' (network) create a             \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m cross-origin escalation path:                                                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Data from Server A can be exfiltrated via Server B's network tool            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m These servers were designed independently but the agent connects to both,    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m creating an"]
[0.000, "o", " unintended bridge between their trust domains.                   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAttack:\u001b[0m 1. Attacker targets the agent with a prompt injection                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Agent uses 'database' to read data                                        \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Agent passes that data to 'web-fetch' for network                         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 4. Cross-origin violation: data crosses trust boundary                       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m The agent acts as a 'confused deputy' — authorized to use both servers       \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m independently, but combining them violates intended isolation.               \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mBlast radius:\u001b[0m Resources of both 'database' and 'web-fetch' become            \u001b[33"]
[0.000, "o", "m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m interconnected through the agent.                                            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mOWASP Agentic:\u001b[0m ASI07 Insecure Inter-Agent Communication · ASI03 Identity &   \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m Privilege Abuse                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[32mFix:\u001b[0m 1. Separate into different agents: one for 'database', another for      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 'web-fetch'                                                                  \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 2. Add cross-server data flow policy (prevent data from one server being     \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m passed to another)                                                           \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m 3. Use separate MCP sessions with different credential scopes                \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m \u001b[2mLocation:\u001b[0m examples/vulnerable-agent/mcp"]
